WEBVTT

00:00:01.370 --> 00:00:02.960
Strike! Out!

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:04.770
That's game!

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:06.700
<i>We won.</i>

00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:09.590
Hikaru!

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:12.950
<i>We were able to win because of Daigo-kun!</i>

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:17.090
<i>And now, I finally feel like 
I'm part of the Dolphins!</i>

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:19.160
Mifune

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:19.160
Tanikawa

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:20.280
Thank you for the game!

00:01:56.220 --> 00:01:58.260
You all did a fine job.

00:01:57.590 --> 00:02:02.220
Mutsuko's Melancholy

00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:00.360
We were hanging on by a thread at the end,

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:02.720
but Satou and Shigeno 
really came through for us.

00:02:03.150 --> 00:02:04.310
Thank you.

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:10.230
Looking back, getting here has been 
a long and arduous journey for the Dolphins.

00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:14.850
I became this team's coach
 two years ago—no, three...

00:02:14.850 --> 00:02:16.940
And now, finally...

00:02:17.230 --> 00:02:22.280
I'm just so happy we finally
 made it past the first round!

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:24.460
Huh?

00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:25.910
Is he seriously crying?

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:30.170
More importantly, Manager, how's Andy doing?

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:36.050
O-Oh, yeah. Fujii called me 
from the hospital earlier.

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:39.090
Thankfully, it looks like 
it was only a light tear.

00:02:39.310 --> 00:02:41.640
But it means he'll be out for ten days.

00:02:42.610 --> 00:02:43.390
Ten days?

00:02:44.090 --> 00:02:48.340
Unfortunately, Andy won't be able to 
wear the mask in next week's game.

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:51.810
So Daigo will be our catcher for it.

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:54.020
Yes, sir!

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:58.240
Hey, Hikaru-kun, you're coming 
next week, too, right?

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:02.200
Huh? Uh, well, if it's all right 
with everyone else...

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:05.200
What? Of course it is.

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:10.240
With two aces on our team, Urabe and you,
we might actually win our second game, too!

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:11.720
Right, Urabe?

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:13.580
Totally.

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:14.670
You <i>have</i> to come.

00:03:15.190 --> 00:03:18.800
If we get past the second round, 
the third round's played on the same day.

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:21.050
Which means we'll need another pitcher.

00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:22.830
However!

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:25.460
Make sure you're prepped next time!

00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:28.970
The set position, pickoffs, base covering,
and dealing with bunts.

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:32.850
There are so many pitching basics 
that you're utterly clueless about!

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:37.260
Today, by some miracle, it all worked out, 
but baseball's not always so forgiving.

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:38.190
Got that?!

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:39.740
Yup!

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:47.580
So, let's all go wolf down some 
barbecue to celebrate our first win!

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:49.070
All right!

00:03:49.070 --> 00:03:50.870
I'm starving.

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:52.750
Barbecue, barbecue!

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:55.190
Uh, Manager?

00:03:55.190 --> 00:03:55.980
Yeah?

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:59.710
The two of us have something we need to do,
so do you mind if we skip?

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:00.770
What?

00:04:00.770 --> 00:04:02.840
The two MVPs aren't joining us?

00:04:03.270 --> 00:04:04.440
Sorry.

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:06.850
There's just something 
we really want to go do.

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:08.900
I see.

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:10.380
Oh, Manager?

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:12.960
I'm off, too.

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:14.650
What? You're going, too, Urabe?

00:04:15.070 --> 00:04:16.910
Man, what a downer.

00:04:20.420 --> 00:04:22.210
Well, it is what it is.

00:04:22.210 --> 00:04:25.120
Just be there for the pre-game
practice on Saturday.

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:26.450
Good job today!

00:04:35.410 --> 00:04:36.300
What's going on?

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:39.060
You're not going with them to have barbecue?

00:04:39.060 --> 00:04:42.380
Yeah, we were thinking 
we could practice nearby for a bit.

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:46.840
Today's game highlighted a lot 
of things we still have to work on.

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:48.640
I asked him if we could.

00:04:49.290 --> 00:04:50.140
Oh.

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:53.590
Okay, I'll go grab you guys 
a couple of boxed lunches.

00:04:53.590 --> 00:04:56.180
You can't do anything on an empty stomach.

00:04:56.180 --> 00:04:57.790
Yeah, that'd be great.

00:05:00.590 --> 00:05:03.030
Hikaru, want me to help you guys practice?

00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:08.540
I'm on commentary duty for 
tonight's game, but I'm free until two.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:12.450
Oh, we'll be fine with just the two of us.

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:15.330
But thank you, Papa.

00:05:17.010 --> 00:05:18.200
All right, then.

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:20.930
Make sure you head home
 before it gets too late.

00:05:20.930 --> 00:05:22.170
Gunma's quite a distance.

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:22.840
Right.

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:24.880
Let's go, Hikaru.

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:26.840
See you.

00:05:27.830 --> 00:05:28.590
Yeah.

00:05:32.050 --> 00:05:36.730
<i>I get it. Both of you have now
tasted the joy of victory.</i>

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:41.880
<i>Looks like you don't have to worry 
about Shigeno Jr. anymore, Goro-kun.</i>

00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:45.800
<i>Just like you and I did back then,</i>

00:05:46.180 --> 00:05:48.750
<i>the two of them have started
chasing that white ball.</i>

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:51.780
BBQ Taiheitei

00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:02.920
I only managed a single hit today.

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:05.150
I didn't do great, either.

00:06:05.150 --> 00:06:07.010
The outfielders didn't 
make any mistakes.

00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:09.430
Maybe that practice game we had paid off.

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:12.020
Sticking around for three years 
paid off, too, didn't it?

00:06:12.020 --> 00:06:14.430
Let's keep it up and 
win in the second round, too!

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:17.070
Nagai, what are you "keeping up" exactly?

00:06:17.070 --> 00:06:20.050
You haven't managed a hit 
since before the practice game.

00:06:20.050 --> 00:06:23.470
It's all good. I'll just get one next time.

00:06:25.140 --> 00:06:27.900
<i>Three years, huh?</i>

00:06:28.380 --> 00:06:31.450
<i>Must be nice. I don't have anywhere 
near that kind of experience.</i>

00:06:32.050 --> 00:06:35.580
<i>Daigo-kun and Hikaru-kun 
both got to play today,</i>

00:06:37.110 --> 00:06:39.460
<i>but I've been sat on the bench this whole time.</i>

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:43.790
Welcome.

00:06:44.290 --> 00:06:45.530
Hello.

00:06:45.530 --> 00:06:46.880
Sorry we're late.

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:49.750
Mind if I sit here?

00:06:51.330 --> 00:06:55.080
They're practicing right now, aren't they?

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:55.950
Yes.

00:06:55.950 --> 00:07:00.140
I saw you giving it your all, too,
 cheering the team on the entire time.

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:01.400
Oh, uh, yeah...

00:07:01.880 --> 00:07:05.020
But it was everyone else 
who got us the victory.

00:07:07.010 --> 00:07:11.130
Must have been kinda boring sitting 
on the sidelines the whole game, huh?

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:15.030
Oh, n-no, it wasn't. Just cheering 
everyone on was a lot of fun for me.

00:07:16.250 --> 00:07:19.410
I used to play for the Dolphins, too.
A long time ago.

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:20.040
Really?

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:24.580
I even played catcher for 
Daigo's father, Shigeno Goro.

00:07:24.580 --> 00:07:26.120
Seriously?!

00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:29.760
I just <i>know</i> that, through hard work and
dedication, a girl can get her chance, too.

00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:34.200
Just keep doing what you're doing, 
and you'll be put in a game, for sure.

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:35.550
Yes, ma'am!

00:07:36.020 --> 00:07:38.030
Oh, look. The meat's done.

00:07:38.030 --> 00:07:39.000
Quick, grab it!

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:40.330
Ah, okay!

00:07:48.910 --> 00:07:49.940
Okay!

00:07:50.760 --> 00:07:53.780
If you can pitch from the stretch like that,
you can prevent stolen bases.

00:07:54.470 --> 00:07:56.870
Yeah, I'm starting to get the hang of it.

00:07:57.150 --> 00:08:00.720
We've just got to work out our signs
and how to deal with bunts.

00:08:00.720 --> 00:08:02.120
But let's take a breather.

00:08:12.590 --> 00:08:13.760
Oh, yeah, this place...

00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:14.640
Huh?

00:08:15.050 --> 00:08:16.890
We haven't been here since then.

00:08:21.820 --> 00:08:23.020
Nice catch!

00:08:24.160 --> 00:08:25.060
Hey!

00:08:26.380 --> 00:08:29.380
Tomorrow's practice session 
will be our battery debut!

00:08:31.030 --> 00:08:35.280
I really did think the practice game
was going to be our battery debut.

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:37.300
I was shocked when it wasn't.

00:08:38.970 --> 00:08:43.810
I know I told you in my letter,
but I just couldn't say it to your face.

00:08:44.430 --> 00:08:45.670
I'm sorry. Really, I am.

00:08:48.820 --> 00:08:50.140
It's fine.

00:08:50.910 --> 00:08:53.920
Because of that moment,
 and because you weren't here,

00:08:54.470 --> 00:08:59.430
I was able to keep training hard
so I could one day catch your pitches.

00:09:01.690 --> 00:09:02.810
It helped me, too.

00:09:03.710 --> 00:09:07.170
Because I went to Gunma and 
tried to forget about baseball,

00:09:07.170 --> 00:09:11.250
it made me realize just how much
I wanted to play baseball.

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:16.760
I was really happy we could 
showcase our battery today.

00:09:16.760 --> 00:09:18.280
And not just today!

00:09:20.780 --> 00:09:24.410
You and I are going to reach our goal!

00:09:24.810 --> 00:09:25.560
Yeah.

00:09:26.730 --> 00:09:27.920
That's right!

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:29.420
Our goal is...

00:09:29.950 --> 00:09:31.420
...to become an invincible battery!

00:09:40.890 --> 00:09:42.780
They're all the damn same.

00:09:42.780 --> 00:09:45.070
Getting so worked up over one victory...

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:49.720
Show a little interest in 
our next opponent, will ya?

00:09:47.270 --> 00:09:49.400
Mifune 
Dolphins

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:51.110
Nijigaoka
 Beetles

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:51.110
Hiyoshi 
Warriors

00:09:54.440 --> 00:09:55.610
Here we go.

00:09:56.070 --> 00:09:59.170
Huh? They're already in the final inning?

00:09:56.740 --> 00:09:57.900
Hiyoshi

00:09:56.740 --> 00:09:57.900
Nijigaoka

00:10:00.290 --> 00:10:01.760
Aw, man.

00:10:01.760 --> 00:10:05.370
I didn't get to see Nijigaoka's batters,
and they're about to win.

00:10:15.990 --> 00:10:16.910
Out!

00:10:17.460 --> 00:10:19.800
What's up with that giant of a pitcher?

00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:22.260
He throws like he's playing catch.

00:10:25.630 --> 00:10:27.350
Not to mention, he looks hella old.

00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:29.650
How does a grade schooler look like that?

00:10:33.430 --> 00:10:33.980
Second!

00:10:37.540 --> 00:10:38.200
Out!

00:10:38.810 --> 00:10:39.850
That's game!

00:10:39.850 --> 00:10:42.410
Yeah!

00:10:43.780 --> 00:10:46.070
Nice pitching, Tamaki!

00:10:46.070 --> 00:10:48.210
Congrats on throwing a no-hitter!

00:10:48.830 --> 00:10:49.810
<i>What?!</i>

00:10:49.810 --> 00:10:52.370
<i>That guy threw a no-hitter?!</i>

00:10:53.700 --> 00:10:56.500
<i>Just who are these guys?</i>

00:11:00.140 --> 00:11:01.460
Nice ball!

00:11:10.340 --> 00:11:12.040
Hey, Sakura!

00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:14.920
Are you busy today?

00:11:14.920 --> 00:11:17.230
Not particularly.

00:11:17.230 --> 00:11:18.740
Then, come with me.

00:11:19.210 --> 00:11:22.900
I want to practice bunting, 
but they're hard to do by yourself.

00:11:22.900 --> 00:11:24.870
Hikaru can't come over on weekdays.

00:11:26.960 --> 00:11:31.610
What's this? In the past, you'd try to
shoo me away every chance you'd get.

00:11:31.610 --> 00:11:36.250
You see me as a convenient girl to run to
when Hikaru-kun and his dad aren't around?

00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:37.040
Huh?

00:11:37.890 --> 00:11:42.010
Well, you <i>did</i> play the entire game
 and had some great moments, it's true.

00:11:42.010 --> 00:11:46.010
There's not much else a benchwarmer like me
can do for you, is there?

00:11:47.500 --> 00:11:48.850
That's not what I was—

00:11:49.040 --> 00:11:51.700
C'mon, I'm joking! 
I'm just messing with you!

00:11:51.700 --> 00:11:54.290
It's fine. Of course it's fine!

00:11:54.290 --> 00:11:57.160
Th-Thank you.

00:12:21.180 --> 00:12:23.680
Okay, I feel like I've got the hang of it now.

00:12:24.140 --> 00:12:25.680
Oh, really?

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:29.810
<i>I'm the one dying here. 
I've thrown nearly a hundred balls.</i>

00:12:30.310 --> 00:12:31.830
Good work, you two.

00:12:31.830 --> 00:12:34.810
I've brought you some cake, 
so why don't you two take a breather?

00:12:34.810 --> 00:12:38.020
Oh, yes! Thank you very much!

00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:45.950
Actually, you know what?

00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:46.930
Huh?

00:12:46.930 --> 00:12:52.080
You can throw pretty well, you can hit,
and you're generally quite sporty.

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:55.960
I think you should be 
given a chance in the team.

00:12:56.820 --> 00:12:59.420
Hikaru and I already got our chance.

00:12:59.730 --> 00:13:02.090
Oh, are you talking about 
what I said earlier?

00:13:02.090 --> 00:13:05.550
Oh, it's fine, it doesn't really bother me.

00:13:06.200 --> 00:13:08.900
I mean, I'd like to be given the chance to play,

00:13:08.900 --> 00:13:12.180
but cheering everyone on is fun, too.

00:13:12.840 --> 00:13:14.060
And...

00:13:14.700 --> 00:13:19.010
If I played, someone from the current 
starting lineup would have to sit out.

00:13:19.890 --> 00:13:23.410
It wouldn't sit right if some girl who'd 
joined right before the tournament...

00:13:23.960 --> 00:13:25.530
took someone's position.

00:13:27.230 --> 00:13:29.600
Oh, wow! You even have a pool.

00:13:29.600 --> 00:13:31.330
Why am I not surprised, rich boy?

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:32.390
Huh?

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:35.210
Urabe!

00:13:35.590 --> 00:13:37.010
I'm coming in.

00:13:37.860 --> 00:13:40.960
Uh, how do you know where I live?

00:13:41.370 --> 00:13:45.080
I asked the kids in your school,
and they all knew.

00:13:45.080 --> 00:13:47.050
I mean, it's Shigeno Goro's house, after all.

00:13:48.040 --> 00:13:50.800
<i>Our private info isn't so private.</i>

00:13:51.300 --> 00:13:54.430
Anyway, I dropped by because 
I wanted to show you something.

00:13:54.980 --> 00:13:56.000
Look at this.

00:13:58.180 --> 00:14:00.000
I was out scouting yesterday.

00:14:02.660 --> 00:14:04.360
Scouting <i>what</i>, exactly?

00:14:04.360 --> 00:14:07.320
Is that the kind of girl 
you're into, Urabe-kun?

00:14:07.800 --> 00:14:08.700
Argh!

00:14:08.940 --> 00:14:10.320
Wrong picture!

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:12.310
Not that one. <i>This</i> one.

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:17.180
He's the ace for the Nijigaoka Beetles, 
our next opponents.

00:14:17.180 --> 00:14:18.100
His name is Tamaki.

00:14:18.860 --> 00:14:22.720
It didn't even occur to you clowns 
to find out who we're playing next,

00:14:22.720 --> 00:14:24.870
so I took it upon myself to check them out.

00:14:25.990 --> 00:14:31.470
Unfortunately, the game was pretty 
much over, so I didn't get much info.

00:14:32.150 --> 00:14:35.900
But what I did find out is that
this beanstalk's Eephus pitch

00:14:35.900 --> 00:14:38.440
helped him throw a no-hitter.

00:14:39.460 --> 00:14:40.770
A no-hitter?

00:14:41.010 --> 00:14:41.740
That's right.

00:14:41.740 --> 00:14:44.380
What? And what did you say his pitch was?

00:14:44.380 --> 00:14:45.680
An Eephus pitch.

00:14:45.680 --> 00:14:46.990
What's that?

00:14:47.510 --> 00:14:49.890
It's essentially a slow ball.

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:53.640
If they're letting the other team 
swing and still pulling off a no-no,

00:14:53.640 --> 00:14:55.950
it means their defense must be top notch.

00:14:56.520 --> 00:15:00.830
And we have to score against a team 
like that without our cleanup, Andy!

00:15:01.110 --> 00:15:05.280
Of course, we'll only need one run,
because I'll be shutting them out!

00:15:05.970 --> 00:15:08.590
Anyway, since we don't have much time,

00:15:09.070 --> 00:15:10.930
let's get started, Shigeno.

00:15:11.930 --> 00:15:13.260
Get started with what?

00:15:13.990 --> 00:15:14.890
Are you braindead?!

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:17.480
Battery practice, of course!

00:15:17.480 --> 00:15:20.670
You haven't even caught 
a single one of my pitches yet!

00:15:20.670 --> 00:15:23.100
We have to get used to 
each other's game and sync up!

00:15:23.390 --> 00:15:26.610
Y-Yeah, you're right. Sorry, sorry.

00:15:27.270 --> 00:15:29.980
<i>Huh. Urabe-kun's so hardworking.</i>

00:15:29.980 --> 00:15:32.160
<i>I like it. This is good!</i>

00:15:39.060 --> 00:15:40.580
<i>Crap.</i>

00:15:41.050 --> 00:15:44.830
<i>I'm wearing the mask, but I totally 
didn't think about our next opponent,</i>

00:15:44.830 --> 00:15:47.470
<i>or the fact that I have to 
get used to Urabe's pitches.</i>

00:15:47.940 --> 00:15:49.710
<i>I don't like Urabe,</i>

00:15:49.710 --> 00:15:54.320
<i>but his attitude towards baseball 
and his skill are leagues above mine!</i>

00:15:56.710 --> 00:15:57.930
Nice ball!

00:16:00.120 --> 00:16:02.890
All right. Now, let's introduce 
Little Miss Bored Benchwarmer...

00:16:03.680 --> 00:16:05.050
Get in the batter's box.

00:16:05.050 --> 00:16:06.560
Who, me?

00:16:06.910 --> 00:16:08.800
Yes, <i>you</i>.

00:16:08.800 --> 00:16:10.500
Get in there, benchwarmer!

00:16:10.500 --> 00:16:13.910
If there's a batter between us, 
it'll be more like the real deal.

00:16:14.240 --> 00:16:16.590
Stop calling me benchwarmer!

00:16:16.590 --> 00:16:18.160
I have a name!

00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:24.770
I'm kinda scared. This is the first time 
I've had anyone pitching at me.

00:16:24.770 --> 00:16:26.150
Do you have a helmet?

00:16:26.150 --> 00:16:27.670
If you're worried, I can go get one.

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:31.050
You won't need one. 
Are you suggesting my control sucks?

00:16:31.050 --> 00:16:33.220
Jeez! You'd better not hit me!

00:16:33.590 --> 00:16:36.460
If you're not happy with just being 
a scarecrow, you can swing, too.

00:16:36.460 --> 00:16:39.600
Foul tips and the ol' swing and a miss 
make for good catching practice.

00:16:39.790 --> 00:16:41.730
Huh? I'm allowed to hit it?

00:16:42.320 --> 00:16:44.690
<i>What's that fool getting so excited about?</i>

00:16:44.690 --> 00:16:46.980
<i>I told her she could swing.</i>

00:16:47.540 --> 00:16:51.570
<i>As if a female rookie could hit 
one of my pitches in a million years!</i>

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:03.040
Watch it! We'll get in trouble 
with the neighbors!

00:17:03.490 --> 00:17:04.730
I'm sorry.

00:17:05.470 --> 00:17:08.460
I can only really hit it straight.

00:17:09.240 --> 00:17:12.840
<i>What the hell?! Where did that 
self-assured swing come from?!</i>

00:17:13.570 --> 00:17:17.410
<i>She's way too good to be warming the bench!</i>

00:17:17.840 --> 00:17:19.760
Mifune Batting 
Center

00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:21.120
Hey!

00:17:22.260 --> 00:17:26.730
Hi, Manager. Sorry for calling you 
out here after you just got off work.

00:17:26.980 --> 00:17:30.540
You guys sure are dedicated, 
practicing your batting on weekdays.

00:17:30.540 --> 00:17:31.860
All right, show me.

00:17:32.130 --> 00:17:34.860
Oh, <i>we're</i> not the ones batting...

00:17:35.460 --> 00:17:37.160
You hear that, don't you?

00:17:39.470 --> 00:17:40.420
What's that noise?

00:17:42.240 --> 00:17:43.830
Who's that batting?

00:17:48.470 --> 00:17:49.330
Sakura?!

00:17:54.790 --> 00:17:56.940
Talk about a surprise.

00:17:56.940 --> 00:17:59.300
I had no idea you were
 such a good batter, Sakura.

00:17:59.580 --> 00:18:04.000
Oh, not really. I can't hit the ball very far.

00:18:04.000 --> 00:18:05.890
I can definitely make good contact, though.

00:18:05.890 --> 00:18:08.320
It's not just her batting, Manager.

00:18:08.320 --> 00:18:09.400
Oh?

00:18:09.400 --> 00:18:11.470
We hit some fungoes down by the river.

00:18:11.470 --> 00:18:15.290
Her arm's good and her legs are solid, 
so she'd have no problem playing defense.

00:18:15.290 --> 00:18:16.300
I understand.

00:18:16.750 --> 00:18:18.860
So what are you saying we should do?

00:18:19.520 --> 00:18:22.050
Put Sakura into the starting 
lineup as an outfielder.

00:18:22.050 --> 00:18:24.990
I think she should be near the 
top of the batting order as well.

00:18:26.600 --> 00:18:28.540
H-Hang on a second...

00:18:29.080 --> 00:18:31.710
What are you planning on doing 
with Hikaru in the next game?

00:18:32.320 --> 00:18:35.220
I was thinking about 
putting him in center field.

00:18:35.220 --> 00:18:39.340
Of course, I need to see how he does in 
the outfield at Saturday's practice first.

00:18:39.590 --> 00:18:42.210
Then, stick Sakura in 
right field or left field!

00:18:42.210 --> 00:18:46.220
You should definitely swap an outfielder out
and put Sakura in instead!

00:18:47.600 --> 00:18:50.480
Our opponent, Nijigaoka, is a defensive team.

00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:54.130
With Andy out, we need 
a lineup that can score us runs.

00:18:57.230 --> 00:18:58.240
All right.

00:18:58.850 --> 00:19:02.810
I'll make my decision about the 
starting lineup after Saturday's practice.

00:19:02.810 --> 00:19:05.660
You guys should focus on 
your own preparations now.

00:19:06.280 --> 00:19:08.580
And head on home. It's getting dark.

00:19:15.240 --> 00:19:17.930
Hey! What did you do that for?!

00:19:17.930 --> 00:19:20.590
I never said I wanted to be 
in the starting lineup!

00:19:21.060 --> 00:19:24.320
Everybody else has been on 
the team since fourth grade!

00:19:24.320 --> 00:19:28.100
Swapping one of them out for me 
when I've only just joined?

00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:30.100
No way! I don't want to be the bad guy!

00:19:30.340 --> 00:19:34.410
What? Then, why did you 
even join the Dolphins?

00:19:34.410 --> 00:19:37.730
Isn't it obvious that you have to play 
your good players if you want to win?

00:19:39.060 --> 00:19:41.360
I'll come right out and say it.

00:19:41.690 --> 00:19:45.780
I <i>need </i>to win two more games
so we can play the Touto Boys!

00:19:45.780 --> 00:19:47.240
Me and Andy together!

00:19:47.650 --> 00:19:50.750
Touto? You mean, the perma-champs?!

00:19:51.370 --> 00:19:55.110
And I can't do it without you guys helping me.

00:19:57.090 --> 00:20:00.700
For Andy's sake as well as my own, 
I simply <i>cannot</i> lose before we meet them.

00:20:01.290 --> 00:20:02.590
So focus!

00:20:05.410 --> 00:20:09.300
<i>I didn't know he had such high aspirations.</i>

00:20:24.130 --> 00:20:28.120
<i>Why... did I join the Dolphins?</i>

00:20:41.150 --> 00:20:42.860
Yes, nice.

00:20:42.860 --> 00:20:45.560
Your pitches from the set position
are good now as well!

00:20:45.560 --> 00:20:46.550
Thank you.

00:20:47.080 --> 00:20:51.390
With pitches like those, you can be our
starting pitcher in the third round.

00:20:51.820 --> 00:20:55.480
He could also come in as a relief pitcher
in round two if Urabe's in bad shape.

00:20:55.800 --> 00:20:56.600
Pfft.

00:20:57.090 --> 00:20:59.570
All right, we're doing 
outfield defense drills next.

00:21:00.060 --> 00:21:02.420
Satou, Sakura, Nagai, Kishimoto!

00:21:02.420 --> 00:21:03.440
Yes, sir!

00:21:06.830 --> 00:21:08.540
Nagai, here it comes!

00:21:08.540 --> 00:21:09.450
Yes!

00:21:13.480 --> 00:21:14.860
Easy, easy!

00:21:15.780 --> 00:21:16.630
Kishimoto!

00:21:16.630 --> 00:21:17.340
Yes!

00:21:19.940 --> 00:21:20.750
All right!

00:21:21.410 --> 00:21:24.280
No surprises from Kishimoto and Nagai.

00:21:24.280 --> 00:21:25.260
Yes.

00:21:25.800 --> 00:21:27.760
All right, next. Satou!

00:21:27.760 --> 00:21:29.050
Thank you!

00:21:30.510 --> 00:21:32.220
Oh, sorry! I hit it too far!

00:21:37.710 --> 00:21:39.270
Nice catch!

00:21:40.780 --> 00:21:42.940
Good. All right, last one, Sakura!

00:21:42.940 --> 00:21:43.900
Yes!

00:21:55.860 --> 00:21:57.460
This is hard.

00:22:04.030 --> 00:22:07.090
<i>I'm okay with this.
This way, I won't be picked.</i>

00:22:07.870 --> 00:22:11.720
<i>I only joined the team because 
I wanted to cheer for Shigeno-kun.</i>

00:22:16.890 --> 00:22:22.020
<i>So I can't take a position away from someone
who's here because they love baseball.</i>

00:22:26.760 --> 00:22:28.820
<i>That idiot!</i>

00:24:00.800 --> 00:24:03.540
Our opponent in the second round
is the Nijigaoka Beetles.

00:24:03.820 --> 00:24:07.530
They're a defense-oriented team, built
around their ace who pitches slow balls.

00:24:07.530 --> 00:24:12.090
On top of that, their manager used to coach 
the Dolphins and was a catcher as well!

00:24:13.410 --> 00:24:15.490
I'm starting to get a bad feeling about this.

00:24:15.490 --> 00:24:19.090
All right. I'm going to show them 
the pride of a new catcher!

00:24:18.060 --> 00:24:25.020
The Experience Level of the Catcher

00:24:19.610 --> 00:24:22.290
Next time: "The Experience 
Level of the Catcher."

00:24:22.290 --> 00:24:24.440
Run to the stage of your dreams!
